From f497a7d685f2db79bf30b44099eae1280c8696a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AMDNR <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 17:08:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix(profile): match a class rule that holds the full
 window class

An Assetto Corsa report (RX 9070) showed the host start, load its effects and
its settings, then write nothing for six minutes while the game ran unscaled:
no scaling attempt, no refusal, no diagnostic code.

GetProfileForWindow normalizes the live window class before comparing it: a WPF
class carries a GUID that changes every run, so
HwndWrapper[AssettoCorsa.exe;;073d6f0b-...] is reduced to AssettoCorsa.exe. The
rule it was compared against held the full class name exactly as the system
reports it, so no profile matched, automatic scaling never fired, and nothing
was written - every refusal and every diagnostic code lives further down, after
the "scaling start" line that was never reached.

Normalize the rule through the same parser before giving up on it. A rule
written by Magpie itself is already normalized and still takes the first, plain
comparison, so nothing changes for it. A rule that holds a live class name now
matches that window, and keeps matching after the application restarts with a
new GUID.

Also name the first few foreground windows that no rule matched, and flush, so
the log can answer "no rule matched this window" instead of being empty. That
line is written only when a profile asks for automatic scaling, at most a few
times per run.

tests/Run-ProfileClassNameRuleTests.ps1 extracts the parser and the match
condition and covers both spellings of a rule, the restart case, the two other
normalized class families, and a near-miss that must not match.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
